# Test: a subsystem the configuration does not use gates nothing
# Spec: plan/immediate/spec-kernel-capability-gate.md AC-5, AC-11
# VALIDATES: on a host whose kernel holds no XFRM dataplane, a configuration that
# installs no Security Association is not gated: ze starts, ze doctor reports
# nothing about IPsec and exits 0, and ze config validate passes.
# PREVENTS: an absent feature nobody asked for reading as a fault. Under a
# refusal an over-reporting predicate stops a router that was working (R-3), and
# this is the shape that would do it: the `vpn { ipsec { } }` block below is
# EMPTY, so it describes no tunnel and installs nothing (AC-11).
#
# The gNMI listener is the readiness fence. It is the daemon saying it got past
# the capability gate, on loopback so no management guard is involved.
option=env:var=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm:value=absent
option=env:var=ze.gnmi.enabled:value=1
option=env:var=ze.gnmi.listen:value=127.0.0.1:19351

tmpfs=ipsec-unused.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
    ipsec {
        interface lo
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json ipsec-unused.conf
expect=exit:code=0
reject=stdout:pattern=doctor-ipsec-xfrm

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate ipsec-unused.conf
expect=exit:code=0
reject=stdout:pattern=config-kernel-capability

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_START
vpn {
    ipsec {
        interface lo
    }
}
EOF_START

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=gNMI server listening on
reject=stderr:pattern=kernel capability
